{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>In the midst of the sea on the dry ground.</b> The meaning of His saying ״in the midst of the sea״ — in its interior; and His saying <b>on the dry ground</b> — that the sea floor was not mud and mire." "<b>And the waters were a wall for them, etc.</b> The meaning is that the portion of the water that was split did not spill to the sides. And His saying ״on their right hand״ is to say that it was not literally a wall that surrounds from all sides:"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:56.363182303Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}